<title>ITALY: CIR to receive 550 bln lire in Valeo sale.</title>
<headline>CIR to receive 550 bln lire in Valeo sale.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>De Benedetti holding CIR said in a statement the sale of Valeo by its subsidiary Cerus would bring CIR a capital gain of 550 billion lire.</p>
<p>&quot;In the framework of the operation...CIR improves its own net consolidated financial position by 1.94 trillion lire, before the capital reimbursement taking place in the first quarter of 1997 for more than 1.0 trillion, of which 500 billion pertains to CIR,&quot; the statement said.</p>
<p>Cerus plans to use the money deriving from the sale to pay back debts and part of the proceeds will be distributed to shareholders.</p>
</text>
